{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "$comment": [
    "The authoritative documentation classification for the repository.",
    "",
    "Before this manifest, document authority was implicit in validator constants:",
    "tools/validate-doc-truth.mjs carried an ACTIVE_DOCS array and a",
    "HISTORICAL_PREFIXES array, so 'which documents may make present-tense claims'",
    "was a fact only the validator source knew. Nothing else could enumerate it, a",
    "new document defaulted to unclassified-and-unchecked, and a superseded",
    "document could still be linked as if it were current.",
    "",
    "This file makes that classification machine-readable and exhaustive. Every",
    "tracked Markdown document that describes the product is listed exactly once.",
    "tools/validate-doc-truth.mjs derives its active/historical sets from here",
    "instead of restating them, and tools/docs-inventory.mjs reports over it.",
    "",
    "Fields, per entry:",
    "",
    "  status      active        describes the system as it is now",
    "              historical    a point-in-time record; true when written, frozen",
    "              superseded    replaced by another document; kept as evidence",
    "              release-record a published release's notes or validation record",
    "",
    "  authority   normative     may be cited as current truth; drift is a defect",
    "              informative   explanatory or contextual; not a truth source",
    "",
    "  appliesTo   the version or release line the document speaks for. Active",
    "              documents use \"current\"; the rest name their own line, so a",
    "              reader never has to infer which release a claim belonged to.",
    "",
    "  replacement the path that supersedes this document, or null. Required to be",
    "              non-null exactly when status is \"superseded\", and required to",
    "              resolve to a file that exists.",
    "",
    "Test fixtures under examples/fixtures/** are deliberately absent: they are",
    "input data for the extraction tests, not documentation about the product.",
    "The unclassified-file report in tools/docs-inventory.mjs excludes them for",
    "the same reason."
  ],
  "excludedPrefixes": ["examples/fixtures/", ".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/", "_dev/"],
  "excludedPaths": [".github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md", "CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md"],
  "documents": [
